      }
    },
    "steps": {
      "type": "uc-buy-steps",
      "blocks": {
        "s1": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Step 01",
            "panel_title": "Research shipping container suppliers.",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/uc-buy-step-illustration-hd.png",
            "fallback_image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1029/2284/6530/files/uc-buy-step-illustration-hd.png",
            "panel_body": "<p>The most important step in the process is finding a <strong>reputable supplier</strong>. Seek out suppliers that offer a high level of transparency every step of the way, from pricing to containers offered to any limitations on pickup or delivery. If you don't want to pore through online searches and directories, start with <strong>Used Conex</strong>. Used Conex offers the largest variety of used containers, the guaranteed lowest prices, and industry-leading warranties on all purchases.</p>"
          }
        },
        "s2": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Step 02",
            "panel_title": "Determine your needs.",
            "fallback_image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1029/2284/6530/files/uc-buy-step2-container.png",
            "panel_body": "<p>Before you even start cost comparisons for new or used shipping containers, think about the purpose for your purchase. Ask yourself the following questions:</p><ul><li>What do I plan on doing with the shipping container?</li><li>Is this shipping container meant for storage or a living space?</li><li>Do I plan on doing any modifications to the container?</li><li>What’s my comfort level as far as scratches, dents, and surface rust?</li><li>Do I need more than one shipping container?</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "s3": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Step 03",
            "panel_title": "How much does a shipping container cost?",
            "fallback_image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1029/2284/6530/files/uc-buy-step3-chart.png",
            "panel_body": "<p>Container pricing varies with size, grade, and how far it has to travel to reach you. Compare quotes across suppliers using the same size and condition so you are comparing like for like, and confirm whether delivery is included in the price you are quoted.</p>"
          }
        },
        "s4": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Step 04",
            "panel_title": "Should you buy a 20ft shipping container or a 40ft shipping container?",
            "fallback_image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1029/2284/6530/files/uc-buy-step4-grades.png",
            "panel_body": "<p>Shipping containers come in a variety of sizes, but the standard is 20 or 40 feet long. Most suppliers also offer standard height or high cube shipping containers with an extra foot of space. Think about your purpose and your budget. What size suits your needs?</p><p>Think about the condition and look of your container. We’ve already mentioned comfort level with dents and dings, but you can also find containers with a fresh coat of paint. If that’s not important to you, you can save money with a container that has faded paint.</p><p>Grading is another area to consider. You’ll typically have three main shipping container types to choose from:</p><p><strong>New, One-Trip:</strong> These are containers that have only seen one trip. They have been loaded with a single cargo and shipped from manufacturing centers overseas and will look practically new.</p><p><strong>Used, Cargo-Worthy (CW):</strong> These are used shipping containers deemed suitable for cargo transportation. They are typically in better shape than wind and water tight containers, but more expensive.</p><p><strong>Used, Wind & Water Tight (WWT):</strong> These are used containers that don’t allow penetration of wind or water but no longer meet CSC (International Convention for Safe Containers) requirements for shipping. They are typically your most affordable option.</p>"
          }
        },
        "s5": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Step 05",
            "panel_title": "Get a quote from the best shipping container company.",
            "fallback_image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1029/2284/6530/files/uc-buy-step5-quote.png",
            "panel_body": "<p>Now that you know the size shipping container you need, start gathering quotes for shipping containers that suit those needs. If you think you may need more than one shipping container, make that decision before gathering quotes. You may be able to get a discount on your total purchase.</p><p>Not sure where to start? Get an instant quote from Used Conex. Our quotes include an option for pickup or delivery.</p>"
          }
        },
        "s6": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Step 06",
            "panel_title": "Arrange transportation for your shipping container.",
            "fallback_image_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/1029/2284/6530/files/uc-buy-step6-delivery.png",
            "panel_body": "<p>Before purchasing a shipping container, delivery customers need to make sure that they meet the delivery guidelines set by their supplier. At Used Conex, we have a delivery guide to ensure a smooth delivery for all our customers.</p><p>Consider building in time for delivery route inspections that could help your supplier (and you!) determine best routes to get your shipping container to where it needs to go. Every supplier should have a checklist for drop site preparation, as well.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "s1",
